refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
boolsocket_getpeername Socketsocket stringaddress intport&null;
Queries the remote side of the given socket which may either result in host/port or in a Unix filesystem path, dependent on its type.

&reftitle.errors;


 A ValueError is thrown if the socket family is not
 AF_UNIX, AF_INET or AF_INET6.

&reftitle.changelog;





    &Version;
    &Description;



   &sockets.changelog.socket-param;


    8.0.0

     A ValueError is now thrown when the socket family is not supported;
     previously an E_WARNING was emitted and &false; was returned.

&reftitle.notes;
socket_getpeername should not be used with AF_UNIX sockets created with socket_accept: the client of such a socket usually has no name. Only connected sockets return meaningful values.
For having socket_getpeername to return a meaningful value, the socket it is applied upon must of course be one for which the concept of "peer" makes sense.
